{
  "name": "Track appointment confirmations and two-way SMS reminders with VoxiSMS and PostgreSQL",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "b0ef844f-201d-8a6c-58db-81141fcc471c",
      "name": "Start here",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -900,
        -1120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 950,
        "height": 1050,
        "content": "## Two-way appointment reminders and confirmation tracking\n\n### Who is this for?\n\nSalons and service businesses that need SMS confirmations and a staff queue for booking requests.\n\n### How it works\n\nAuthenticated booking webhooks update PostgreSQL. Every five minutes, the workflow checks local sending hours, consent and opt-outs, then reserves one reminder attempt per booking revision before sending through VoxiSMS.\n\nYES with a reference confirms; CANCEL and RESCHEDULE create staff requests. STOP suppresses future reminders. Bare replies match only one eligible appointment; ambiguous replies go to staff. Event deduplication and atomic reservations protect against repeated processing and overlapping runs.\n\n### Setup and requirements\n\nFollow the [setup guide](https://voxisms.com/integrations/n8n/appointment-reminders) and install the [SQL schema](https://voxisms.com/downloads/n8n/appointment-reminders/v1/schema.sql). Select PostgreSQL credentials on all six database nodes, VoxiSMS credentials on both SMS nodes, and Header Auth on booking intake.\n\nRequires PostgreSQL 15+ with verified TLS, the verified VoxiSMS node, and an Android SMS line. Supports self-hosted n8n and n8n Cloud where verified community nodes are enabled. Database, n8n, VoxiSMS and carrier charges may apply.\n\n### Customize and launch\n\nSet businessId in all three configuration nodes; adjust database reminder windows and sending hours. Start in dry run, complete the guide\u2019s controlled tests, and assign staff to monitor the queue before activation.\n\nStaff must process cancellation/rescheduling in the booking system. API acceptance is not delivery; uncertain sends are held without automatic retries."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "64e6f3ee-f25a-8089-2c3f-ec297d7f4318",
      "name": "Booking explanation",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        100,
        -700
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1080,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "## 1. Keep booking state current\nPOST externalId, customerName, phone, startsAt, timezone, smsConsent and sourceUpdatedAt. The booking system must send authenticated updates for new bookings, time/phone changes, cancellation and completion. Timestamps require an offset; phones require international E.164 format.\n\nOlder updates are ignored. Changed time/phone rotates the reply reference. CANCEL by SMS is only a request; the booking source sends action=cancel after staff processes it. Dry run validates but does not store bookings."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
