    {
      "id": "3aae06e7-3cf2-89b5-d5a9-5b41bf692ded",
      "name": "Reply explanation",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -580,
        840
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 650,
        "height": 520,
        "content": "## 3. Match replies safely\nThe verified VoxiSMS Trigger checks the webhook signature. SQL additionally checks the customer ID and receiving line, then de-duplicates eventId in the same transaction as the booking update.\n\nYES + reference confirms. CANCEL / RESCHEDULE + reference creates a staff request. STOP suppresses future reminders on this business line. Commands are case-insensitive; extra prose goes to staff.\n\nA bare command matches only one future, recently reminded appointment for the sender. Multiple matches are escalated. Old references, wrong senders and out-of-order replies cannot overwrite bookings. No automatic reply SMS is sent.\n\nMonitor failed n8n executions as well as the staff queue. Provider retries are not a substitute for handling downstream database errors."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
